    "lawCode": "Add §1202-aa, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1086\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the city of\nWhite Plains to impose an occupancy tax\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL :\n\nAuthorizes the imposition by the City of White Plains of a tax of up\nto three percent of the per diem rental rate, subject to certain\nexceptions, upon persons occupying any room for hire in any hotel\nwithin its jurisdiction for the period expiring December 31, 2012.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nThe tax law is amended by adding a new section 1202-z which authorizes\nthe City of White Plains to impose a tax of up to three percent of the\nper diem rental rate upon persons occupying any room for hire in any\nhotel within its jurisdiction for the period expiring December 31,\n2010, subject to certain exceptions.\n\nSection 2 states the effective date, which is immediately.\n\n EFFECTS OF THE PRESENT LAW WHICH THE BILL WILL ALTER :\n\nThis bill authorizes the City of White Plains to impose a tax of up to\nthree percent of the per diem rental rate, subject to certain\nexceptions, upon persons occupying any room for hire in any hotel\nwithin its jurisdiction for the period expiring December 31, 2012.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill will permit the City of White Plains to impose a tax of up\nto three percent of the per diem rental rate, subject to certain\nexceptions, upon persons occupying any room for hire in any hotel\nwithin its jurisdiction for the period expiring December 31, 2012.\nOther neighboring cities have recently imposed these taxes including\nthe City of Rye and New Rochelle.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nA.9678/S.6795 of 2007-2008 - Passed Assembly\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
